<title>UK: World Bank ups 25yr zero-coupon bond to 7 bln rand.</title>
<headline>World Bank ups 25yr zero-coupon bond to 7 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased for the third time by lead manager J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WORLD BANK</p>
<p> AMT   *7.0 BLN RAND  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    01.APR.22</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  4.125     PAY DATE    01.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  35 BP     REOFFER    3.90	SPREAD	=</p>
<p> NOTES	*ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 2.0 BLN RAND ON 11.MAR.97</p>
<p>		INCREASED BY 2.0 BLN RAND ON 13.MAR.97</p>
<p>		INCREASED BY 1.0 BLN RAND ON 14.MAR.97</p>
<p>		INCREASED BY 2.0 BLN RAND ON 25.MAR.97</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 5-50-500  SALE LIMITS US/UK/ZA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SUPRA     TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    12.5 BP   SELL CONC  22.5 BP   PRAECIP     =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
